WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.730
Look at a bright red shirt
through a sheet of blue filter.

2
00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:07.290
The shirt suddenly looks
black, or very nearly.

3
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.930
Take the filter away,
and it's red again.

4
00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:11.870
The shirt hasn't changed at all,

5
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.930
and neither has the light in the room.

6
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.630
So why does it look
black through the filter?

7
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.830
In this mission, you'll find out
what decides the colour of an

8
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:23.110
object, and what a colour
filter really does to light.

9
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:27.350
You'll also compare how convex
and concave lenses bend rays of

10
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:27.590
light.

11
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:32.250
Your mission: find out why
the red shirt looks black.
